# Tutorial 22 — Phone Storytelling
# Reference: docs/guides/vns-by-example/12-phone-storytelling.md
# Read scripts/tutorial/README.md for the complete course and linked references.
@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_22
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: The phone is a story model with contacts, apps, threads, messages, unread state, media, and calls. The UI presents that model.
@label lesson_menu
> Receive a workshop message -> message
> Contacts, apps and calls -> structure
> Save and replay phone events -> practice
> Checkpoint -> checkpoint
> Finish and return to the hub -> return_hub
@label message
[phone contact lavender name="Lavender"]
[phone thread workshop title="Workshop" participants=player,lavender]
[if !tutorial_phone_sent]
[phone message workshop lavender "A small message from the white page." time=10:20]
[flag tutorial_phone_sent]
[endif]
[phone unread workshop true]
Lavender: Open the thread, read the message, then close the phone with its back control.
[phone open chat workshop]
Lavender: A guarded story event sends the message once per state history. Reopening this lesson does not duplicate it.
[phone close]
[phone unread workshop false]
[jump lesson_menu]
@label structure
Lavender: The seed file is {b}config/phone/phone.properties{/b}. Put stable contacts and app structure there; put new story events in VNS commands.
narrator: [phone message workshop type=image asset="assets/phone/clue.png" caption="A clue"]
Lavender: That media command is an example. Add the actual image before executing it. Audio and video messages likewise need real assets and a supported runtime.
narrator: [phone call workshop_call title="Lavender" participant=lavender video=false]
narrator: [phone open call workshop_call]
Lavender: Defining a call record and opening it are separate operations. Use stable record IDs even when display names are translated.
[jump lesson_menu]
@label practice
Lavender: Exercise: add a second contact and thread, send a text clue, and branch after the player reads it. Then add an image you created yourself.
Lavender: Save before and after receiving the clue. Load both saves, roll back, and check message ordering, unread badges, and which event flags were restored.
Lavender: A plain dialogue line that says a phone rang is still useful when an overlay would interrupt the scene's pace.
[jump lesson_menu]
@label checkpoint
Lavender: Where does an incoming message at a specific story beat belong?
> In a VNS phone command -> correct
> Only in the permanent seed file -> retry
@label retry
Lavender: Seed files establish initial structure. A story-time message should be driven by the story.
[jump checkpoint]
@label correct
Lavender: Yes. Separate initial data from events that depend on player progress.
[jump return_hub]

@label return_hub
[phone close]
[if !tutorial_done_22]
[flag tutorial_done_22]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[goto {{HUB_TARGET}}:topics_page_4]
